# Braille Lite add-on (NVDA 2024.4 and later): send "?" itself to the synthesizer at every symbol level.
# NVDA only sends a "?" that ends a sentence (a letter before it, a space or the line's end after it), so in
# "how are you??" both marks were dropped, and the unit, which raises its pitch once per "?", never saw them.
# The word and the level stay NVDA's own ("-").
symbols:
?	-	-	always
